        <IncidentResponseSecurityOntology:hasPlaybookDescription> Setup Import the workflow from the Rapid7 Extension Library and proceed through the Import Workflow wizard in InsightConnect. Import plugins, create or select connections, and rename the workflow as a part of the Import Workflow wizard as necessary. There are three workflow parameters you will need to configure in order to complete setup of your workflow:* `Automox Organization ID`: The identifier of the Automox organization.* `CVEs in Scope`: Comma separated list of CVEs in scope for immediate remediation between InsightVM and Automox.* `Auto-Approve Tasks`: Whether to auto-approve and apply patches for identified vulnerabilities immediately. </IncidentResponseSecurityOntology:hasPlaybookDescription>
        <IncidentResponseSecurityOntology:hasPlaybookID>p582</IncidentResponseSecurityOntology:hasPlaybookID>
        <IncidentResponseSecurityOntology:hasPlaybookName>Orchestrate Automox Vulnerability Sync with Rapid7 InsightVM</IncidentResponseSecurityOntology:hasPlaybookName>
    </owl:NamedIndividual>
    


